# Default deny, then allow back the three parts that are the merge work.
#
# The other direction — listing what to exclude — is how secrets get committed.
# The legacy grapout.com dump that sits beside these folders keeps its
# production credentials in ordinary source files, copied across more of them
# than anyone can audit by reading, and a git history cannot be edited
# afterwards. So nothing is tracked unless it is named here.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/crm/
!/trade/
!/_run/

# ── Things that can be reinstalled ─────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
vendor/
.next/
crm/apps/api/dist/

# ── Live data. Not ours to publish. ────────────────────────────────────────
# A copy of the CRM's database: real clients, real contacts, real messages.
.pgdata/
trade/apibase/storage/framework/
trade/apibase/storage/logs/
trade/apibase/storage/app/public/
_run/logs/

# ── Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

# ── Noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.log
